-----------------------------------
Intro
-----------------------------------

We are a team building an online hat store. The feature being tested allows users to filter products based on price, color, style, and availability.

The participant will act as a customer browsing for a hat. They should think out loud while interacting with the prototype and explain their thoughts before taking actions.

-----------------------------------
Tasks
-----------------------------------

Task 1:
You are looking for a hat within a specific budget. Try to find hats that match your price range.

Task 2:
You have a specific color and style in mind. Try to find a hat that matches those preferences.

Task 3:
You only want to see hats that are currently available for purchase. Try to adjust the results to match this requirement.

-----------------------------------
Notes
-----------------------------------

Participant 1:

Initially scrolled through products instead of using filters
Took time to notice where filtering options were located
Used price filter but was unsure if it applied automatically
Expected results to update instantly

Participant 2:

Used multiple filters at once (color + style + price)
Became confused when no products appeared after filtering
Looked for a way to reset filters
Expected clearer indication of selected filters
-----------------------------------
Feedback
-----------------------------------

Participant 1:

Wanted filters to be more noticeable at first glance
Expected automatic updates without needing extra steps
Suggested clearer labeling for price selection

Participant 2:

Found filtering useful but confusing when results disappeared
Wanted a message explaining why no products were shown
Expected an easy way to remove or reset filters
-----------------------------------
Results
-----------------------------------

Issue 1: Confusion when no results appear

Users thought the site was broken when nothing showed
Quote: “Did it just stop working?”
Hypothesis: No feedback when filters return zero results
Remedy: Add a message like “No items match your filters” and suggest changes

Issue 2: Unclear if filters are applied

Users were unsure if selections were working
Quote: “Did it apply or do I need to press something?”
Hypothesis: Lack of real-time feedback
Remedy: Enable instant updates and highlight active filters clearly

Issue 3: Difficulty resetting filters

Users struggled to return to original results
Quote: “How do I undo this?”
Hypothesis: Reset option is not visible enough
Remedy: Add a clear “Clear All Filters” button
-----------------------------------
Updates (Based on Feedback)
-----------------------------------
Implemented “No results found” message with suggestions
Added “Clear All Filters” button
Displayed active filters clearly at the side of the page
